<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom says Internet loss making legal.</title>
<headline>Telecom says Internet loss making legal.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom Corp said on Wednesday that loss making in its Internet business was a legitimate business strategy.</p>
<p>&quot;It is in the nature of start-up businesses to run at a loss,&quot; Telecom spokesman Clive Litt said.</p>
<p>He was responding to the Commerce Commission's earlier statement that Telecom's Xtra Internet services raised competition concerns.</p>
<p>Telecom welcomed the fact that the commission had dismissed two other Internet pricing issues raised by competing Internet Service Providers. -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
